<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><!--
   Backup rules for API 29–30. These devices predate dataExtractionRules
   (API 31+, see data_extraction_rules.xml) and read fullBackupContent instead,
   so the API-key exclusion has to be stated a second time here — the two files
   are not alternatives, they cover different OS versions. Change one, change
   the other, or Android 10/11 users silently get the weaker behaviour.

   Same reasoning as the API 31+ rules: llm_providers holds the user's LLM API
   keys, encrypted with a non-exportable hardware-backed Keystore key. Restored
   ciphertext could never be decrypted on the new device anyway
   (LlmProviderStore.load() catches the failure and resets to empty), so
   backing it up would ship key material off-device for zero benefit. Excluded,
   the user re-enters their keys — same end state, nothing leaves.

   Links themselves remain backed up.
-->
<full-backup-content>
    <exclude domain="sharedpref" path="llm_providers.xml" />
</full-backup-content>
